# Keep the original fork controller's live state, frozen snapshots, request
# bodies, prompts, raw GitHub responses and local tools out of Git.
#
# Frozen 4,000-repository study: only the safe, derived published summaries
# below may be committed. Batch IDs are dynamic; any valid --batch-id uses
# results/<batch-id>/published/. The four member assignments are maintained
# separately in evaluation/assignments/ and are committed with the study.
#
# Never stage results/<batch-id>-rNNNN/ checkpoints or .tools/ (legacy
# third-party installers). They may contain credentials, original workflows,
# prompts, and raw responses. Run the preview-first workspace reset to discard
# abandoned development data; do not force-add ignored files.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!*/
*/**
!*/published/
*/published/**
!*/published/attempts.csv
!*/published/attempts_4000.csv
!*/published/manifest.json
!*/published/trials/
*/published/trials/**
# Trial summaries are r0001.json through r1000.json (four ASCII digits).
# No arbitrary JSON or secret-bearing artifacts are allowed in published/trials.
!*/published/trials/r[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].json
